            <ArticleTitle>Giant aneurysm of aortocoronary saphenous vein graft compressing the left pulmonary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a case report of a 78-year-old patient with a 7-cm aneurysm of the saphenous vein graft that was used 17 years before to perform a coronary artery bypass grafting on the circumflex artery. CT scan displayed a mass with an internal lumen compressing the left atrium as well as the left pulmonary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
